# REST API conventions

Use when creating or reviewing routes, controllers, schemas, OpenAPI, or endpoint examples.

Works with `http-api.mdc` (Zod/OpenAPI), `role-based-access.mdc` (RBAC/IDOR), `response-contracts.mdc` (DTO envelopes), `search-query-guidelines.mdc`, `api-protection.mdc`.

## Core principle

URLs identify **resources**. HTTP methods describe the action.

```http
GET /users          POST /users
GET /users/{userId}  PATCH /users/{userId}  DELETE /users/{userId}
```

Avoid verb routes: `/getUsers`, `/createUser`, `/users/{userId}/delete`.

## Resource naming & URL formatting

| Rule | Do | Don't |
| ---- | -- | ----- |
| Nouns, plural | `/products`, `/orders` | `/product`, `/getProducts` |
| Lowercase + hyphens | `/email-templates` | `/emailTemplates`, `/Email_Templates` |
| No trailing slash | `/users` | `/users/` |
| No file extension | `Accept: application/json` | `/users.json` |
| IDs in path | `/orders/{orderId}` | `/orders?id=123` |
| Descriptive params | `/users/{userId}/posts/{postId}` | `/users/{id}/posts/{id}` |

Nest only for clear ownership; keep nesting shallow (≤ 2 levels). Prefer `/posts/{postId}/comments` over deep org→team→project→task trees.

Mount in `src/app/router.ts`. No `/api/v1` by default — `platform-patterns.mdc`.

## Audience prefixes (no redundant CRUD)

| Prefix | Audience | Examples |
| ------ | -------- | -------- |
| *(app)* | Client/customer | `GET /brands`, `POST /uploads/presign` |
| `/me` | Current actor | `GET /me`, `PATCH /me` |
| `/employee` | Internal staff | `GET /employee/tickets` |
| `/admin` | Platform admins | `GET /admin/organizations` |

One resource = one path per audience. Do **not** clone the same list under `/admin`, `/employee`, and app. Self data → `/me`, not `/users/{userId}`. Details: `role-based-access.mdc`.

## HTTP methods

| Method | Use |
| ------ | --- |
| `GET` | Read |
| `POST` | Create or non-idempotent action |
| `PUT` | Full replace |
| `PATCH` | Partial update (preferred) |
| `DELETE` | Delete |

Non-CRUD: model as a resource (`POST /exports`, `GET /exports/{exportId}`) — not `POST /runExport`.

## Common query parameters

Aligned with `src/lib/pagination.schema.ts` (`paginatedQuerySchema`):

| Parameter | Use | Template default |
| --------- | --- | ---------------- |
| `page` | 1-based page number | `1` |
| `limit` | Page size (max 100) | `20` |
| `sort` | Allowlisted sort field | per-resource enum |
| `order` | `asc` \| `desc` | `desc` |
| `search` | Free-text search | optional; prefer `min(2)` |
| Resource fields | Filters (`status`, `createdAfter`, …) | list schema only |

```http
GET /products?category=shoes&page=2&limit=20&sort=price&order=asc&search=runner
```

**Do not use** as aliases: `pageSize`, `per_page`, `q`, `sortBy`, `direction`.  
**Do not expose** `offset` or `cursor` as public query params — offset is computed via `pageToOffset` inside services. Cursor pagination only if a product explicitly adopts it later.

Lists return `{ items, meta }` via `buildPaginationMeta` — `http-api.mdc`.

## Status codes

| Status | Use |
| ------ | --- |
| `200` | Read/update with body |
| `201` | Created |
| `202` | Accepted (async job) |
| `204` | Success, no body |
| `400` | Malformed request |
| `401` | Missing/invalid auth |
| `403` | Authenticated but not allowed |
| `404` | Missing or not visible (incl. wrong tenant/owner) |
| `409` | Conflict |
| `422` | Validation failed (`VALIDATION_ERROR`) |
| `429` | Rate limited |
| `500` | Unexpected server error |

## Response & security

Envelope and errors: `response-contracts.mdc`, `docs/api-response-samples.md` — `{ success, message, data?, meta?, code?, errors? }`. Do not invent a second envelope.

AuthZ: authenticate protected routes; authorize by role, ownership, and tenant (`role-based-access.mdc`, `multi-tenant-safety.mdc`). Validate all input (`http-api.mdc`). Rate-limit sensitive endpoints (`api-protection.mdc`).

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Nouns, plural, lowercase, hyphenated; no trailing slash or `.json`
- [ ] Correct audience prefix; no duplicate role CRUD
- [ ] Methods match operation; non-CRUD modeled as resources
- [ ] List query uses `page`/`limit`/`sort`/`order`/`search`
- [ ] Status codes + project response envelope
- [ ] AuthN/AuthZ + object scope; OpenAPI regenerated
